# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# The Debian packages the desktop adds to nyra-base, one per line: the package, then why it is here.
# apt installs them without recommends from the snapshot of the pinned base (docs/IMAGE.md); their
# dependencies come with them and are listed in the SBOM. A package enters only with a reason.
sddm                  the login screen (display manager), started at boot
sddm-theme-breeze     the look of the login screen, Plasma's own (Breeze)
plymouth              the boot and shutdown screen (docs/IMAGE.md, "Boot screen"): shows the Nyra theme, then hands the screen to SDDM
plymouth-label        text rendering that plymouth's script themes need: without it plymouthd crashes as soon as it runs the Nyra theme
kwin-wayland          the compositor of the Plasma session, and of the login screen (Wayland, no X server)
plasma-workspace      the Plasma session: plasmashell, startplasma-wayland and the session SDDM offers
plasma-desktop        the desktop itself: panel, application launcher, desktop and task manager
qt6-wayland           Qt's Wayland platform plugin, which every Qt program of the session needs
dbus-user-session     the user's D-Bus session bus, started by systemd, which the Plasma session uses
konsole               the terminal, the one KDE application that stays in the desktop
fonts-noto-core       Noto Sans, Plasma's default font, and the fonts of Arabic, Hebrew, the Indic and South-East Asian scripts, Greek, Cyrillic and the other alphabets
fonts-noto-cjk        Chinese, Japanese and Korean glyphs, which no other font of the list has
locales-all           every glibc locale precompiled, so the user picks a language without the network and without locale-gen
hunspell-en-us        English spelling dictionary of KDE's text fields (Sonnet); the dictionaries of other languages are on demand
hunspell-ro           Romanian spelling dictionary of the same text fields
libgl1-mesa-dri       Mesa's OpenGL drivers, with llvmpipe for machines without a GPU driver
libegl-mesa0          Mesa's EGL, which KWin renders with
udisks2               mounts removable media (an SD card) for the logged-in user, under /run/media/<user>/<label>
pipewire              the sound server, started per user by systemd on first use
pipewire-bin          pw-cat (pw-play, pw-record), the command line player and recorder the audio test uses
pipewire-pulse        PipeWire's PulseAudio socket, which Plasma's volume control and most programs talk to
pipewire-alsa         routes programs that use ALSA directly through PipeWire
wireplumber           PipeWire's session manager: makes a sink and a source of every sound card
cups                  the print system (the scheduler, driverless IPP printers, lp, lpadmin)
cups-filters          turns text and PDF into what a printer takes, so a page printed from any program arrives
ffmpeg                the video decoders (H.264 and the rest of libavcodec); also what the video test decodes with
